save visited_errors = false

Welcome to the Error Examples exhibit!
I'll help you understand common Bobbin mistakes.

- Indentation errors
    The most common issue: using TABS instead of SPACES.
    Bobbin requires spaces for indentation.
    In Godot: Edit > Indentation > Convert Indent to Spaces
    Check the bottom-right corner of the editor for current mode.

- Undefined variables
    If you see a variable show as blank or cause an error...
    Make sure you declared it with save, temp, or extern FIRST.
    Declaration must come BEFORE any usage in the file.

- Missing extern values
    If an extern variable shows as empty or undefined...
    Check that host_state is being passed when starting dialogue.
    The Oracle NPC shows the correct pattern for this.

- Dialogue not advancing
    If dialogue seems stuck, check the console for errors.
    Common cause: runtime failed to load due to syntax error.
    Also check: is the .bobbin file path correct?

- Choices not appearing
    Make sure choices use dash-space: "- Choice text"
    And responses are indented with SPACES below.
    Each choice needs at least one line of response.

set visited_errors = true

Remember: Check the Godot console for error messages!
They usually point to the exact line with the problem.
